<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duan Qirui</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1865">1865</a>–<a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tuan Chi-jui</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duan Qirui was a Chinese general and politician, a protégé of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai">Yuan Shikai</a> and leader of the Anhui clique of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-army">Beiyang Army</a>. He served several times as premier of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-government">Beiyang government</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> in 1917 and took large Japanese loans. Defeated in 1920, he returned as provisional chief executive from 1924 to 1926.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duan-qirui.jpg" alt="Duan Qirui" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DuanQirui.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
